---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
import Chip from './Chip.astro';

const weights = [
  { label: 'Light', n: 5 },
  { label: 'Style', n: 4 },
  { label: 'Walking', n: 2 },
  { label: 'Crowds', n: 3 },
  { label: 'Variety', n: 3 },
  { label: 'Icons', n: 1 },
];
const days = Array.from({ length: 15 }, (_, i) => (i < 5 ? 'gz' : i < 7 ? 'sz' : 'hk'));
const mock = 'flex min-h-[236px] flex-col gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface-2 p-4';
const label = 'm-0 font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.08em] text-muted uppercase';
---

<section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title" class="scroll-mt-4 border-b border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <SectionHead id="how-title" kicker="How it works" title="Four steps from brief to route">
      <p>
        PhotoRouter has no built-in agent. It writes the prompt, your own AI writes the plan, and PhotoRouter checks the plan and
        shows it on the map.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>

    <ol class="mt-12 grid list-none gap-5 p-0 md:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="flex flex-col rounded-[22px] border border-line bg-surface p-4 shadow-card sm:p-5">
        <div class={mock} aria-hidden="true">
          <p class={label}>Gear</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            <Chip on>2 bodies</Chip><Chip on>16-35 mm</Chip><Chip on>70-200 mm</Chip><Chip on>Tripod</Chip><Chip on>ND 6 + 10</Chip><Chip>Drone</Chip>
          </div>
          <p class={label}>Photography</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            <Chip on>Street</Chip><Chip on>Night</Chip><Chip on>Long exposure</Chip><Chip>Landscape</Chip><Chip on>Heritage</Chip>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <p class={label}>Pace</p>
            <span class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-line bg-surface p-0.5 text-[11.5px] font-semibold">
              <span class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-muted">Relaxed</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-ink px-2.5 py-0.5 text-surface">Balanced</span>
              <span class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-muted">Packed</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="m-0 mt-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-3 py-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
            Weekdays 09:00-18:00. Must see: Shamian Island. Skip: Huaqiangbei.<span class="blink text-ink">|</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="t-accent font-display text-3xl leading-none font-extrabold">01</span>
          <h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-bold">Describe the trip</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          A form for your gear (bodies, lenses, tripod, ND filters, drone) and the photography you like: street, night,
          cityscape, architecture, heritage, long exposure, landscape and more. Set the pace, how much walking you want, your
          working hours on weekdays, whether to avoid crowds, must-see and skip spots, and add a free-text description.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="flex flex-col rounded-[22px] border border-line bg-surface p-4 shadow-card sm:p-5">
        <div class={mock} aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <p class={label}>Priorities</p>
            <span class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-line bg-surface p-0.5 text-[11.5px] font-semibold">
              <span class="rounded-full bg-ink px-2.5 py-0.5 text-surface">Chat</span>
              <span class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-muted">API</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
            {
              weights.map((w) => (
                <>
                  <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink">{w.label}</span>
                  <span class="flex gap-1">
                    {[1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((i) => (
                      <span class:list={['h-2 flex-1 rounded-full', i <= w.n ? 'bg-accent' : 'bg-line']} />
                    ))}
                  </span>
                </>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <p class="m-0 mt-auto border-t border-line pt-3 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            brief · trip frame · 42 spots · schema
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="t-accent font-display text-3xl leading-none font-extrabold">02</span>
          <h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-bold">Build the prompt</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Pick a preset, a voice and weighted priorities for light, style, walking, crowds, variety and icons. Add optional
          rules, choose the cities to cover, the answer language and extra instructions. The prompt holds your brief, the trip
          frame (dates, cities, train legs, the time slots each day allows) and a catalog of 42 spots with their light, focal
          ranges, tripod needs, effort and crowd levels.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 mb-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Chat</strong> puts the JSON Schema inside the prompt, ready to paste into any
          assistant. <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">API</strong> leaves it out so the schema can go into your
          provider's structured-output option.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="flex flex-col rounded-[22px] border border-line bg-surface p-4 shadow-card sm:p-5">
        <div class={mock} aria-hidden="true">
          <pre class="code m-0 overflow-hidden text-ink">{'{'}
  <span class="k">"date"</span>: <span class="s">"2026-11-17"</span>,
  <span class="k">"slots"</span>: [{'{'}
    <span class="k">"label"</span>: <span class="s">"Before work"</span>,
    <span class="k">"spotId"</span>: <span class="s">"shamian"</span>,
    <span class="k">"note"</span>: <span class="n">null</span>
  {'}'}, …]
{'}'}</pre>
          <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-line pt-3 text-xs font-semibold">
            <span class="inline-flex h-6 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-line bg-surface px-2.5 text-ink">
              <span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-sz"></span>Schema valid
            </span>
            <span class="inline-flex h-6 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-line bg-surface px-2.5 text-ink">0 errors</span>
            <span class="lt-day inline-flex h-6 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-line bg-surface px-2.5 text-ink">
              <span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-(--c)"></span>1 warning
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="t-accent font-display text-3xl leading-none font-extrabold">03</span>
          <h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-bold">Run it in your own AI</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Copy the prompt into any AI assistant, or send it through an API. Paste the JSON it returns back into PhotoRouter, which
          validates the answer against the schema and the trip rules. Errors block the import; warnings are shown with the plan.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="flex flex-col rounded-[22px] border border-line bg-surface p-4 shadow-card sm:p-5">
        <div class={mock} aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 300 92" class="block h-auto w-full">
            <path d="M14 70 C 70 66, 90 30, 150 34 S 240 18, 286 22" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
            <path d="M14 70 C 70 66, 90 30, 150 34 S 240 18, 286 22" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
            <path d="M14 70 C 70 66, 90 30, 150 34 S 240 18, 286 22" pathLength="1000" class="train" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"></path>
            <circle cx="14" cy="70" r="6" class="c-gz" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--c)" stroke-width="3"></circle>
            <circle cx="150" cy="34" r="6" class="c-sz" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--c)" stroke-width="3"></circle>
            <circle cx="286" cy="22" r="6" class="c-hk" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--c)" stroke-width="3"></circle>
          </svg>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-accent text-accent-ink">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="size-3.5"><path d="M5 3.5v9l7.5-4.5Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 gap-[3px]">
              {
                days.map((c, i) => (
                  <span class:list={[`c-${c}`, 'h-5 flex-1 rounded-[4px] bg-(--c)', i === 1 ? 'outline-2 outline-offset-1 outline-ink' : 'opacity-60']} />
                ))
              }
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="m-0 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] text-muted uppercase">Tue 17 Nov · Guangzhou · 2 stops</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="t-accent font-display text-3xl leading-none font-extrabold">04</span>
          <h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-bold">Play the route</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The plan opens on a 3D map with a timeline that scrubs day by day. The camera follows the train legs, walks between
          stops and orbits each one on arrival. Day sheets list every stop's light window, the kit to pack and the Chinese name
          to copy for a taxi.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
